      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Managed conservation often imposes human preferences onto ecosystems, leading to interventions that can unintentionally disrupt natural processes. This anthropocentric approach frequently focuses on maintaining specific species populations rather than restoring functional ecological integrity. Rewilding, by contrast, prioritizes restoring self-regulating natural systems, allowing ecological dynamics to unfold without constant human management. Therefore, a shift towards rewilding represents a necessary evolution beyond outdated control-based conservation models.",
      "source": "target",
