      "content": "To appeal to conservative reviewers, it is strategically better to frame the current model as inadequate rather than aggressively dismissive. Instead of labeling it \"regressive,\" focus on the scientific limitations of interventionism, highlighting that human management often leads to ecological simplification. Assert that the current piecemeal approach fails to address systemic ecological functionality, presenting rewilding as the *next scientifically validated step*. This frames your proposal not as an ideological shift, but as a necessary, evidence-based upgrade to outdated methodologies.",
